Subject: [PATCH 1/2] claude: Keep the mail outbox out of the trunk rebase
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: qslspvuqlpyrzqvzlrwmnxumktwzwlkv

Step 1 of process-email rebased every commit of yours that was not on
trunk, on mail, or descended from the new mail tip. An outbox built on
an older mail tip matched none of those, so after a fetch that moved
mail, the outbox and the mail working copy were rebased onto trunk.
The mail workspace then held trunk's files, and pushing the bookmark
would have offered Pat trunk history as mail.

Trunk and mail share no commit but the root, so excluding every
descendant of mail's history leaves out the outbox wherever it sits.
---
change-id: qslspvuqlpyrzqvzlrwmnxumktwzwlkv

 .claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
index 82fb47b..d29e701 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
@@ -51,10 +51,12 @@ one fetch covers them:
     jj git fetch --all-remotes
 
 **Trunk.** Rebase your unmerged trunk work onto the new trunk. The
-revset is your commits that are on neither branch upstream and not
-part of your mail outbox:
+revset is your commits that are not on trunk upstream and not on the
+list's history. Trunk and the list share no commit but `root()`, so
+everything descended from the list, your outbox included, is left out
+however far the list has moved since you built on it:
 
-    work='mine() ~ ::trunk@upstream ~ ::mail@upstream ~ mail@upstream::'
+    work='mine() ~ ::trunk@upstream ~ (::mail@upstream ~ root())::'
     jj rebase -s "roots(${work})" -d trunk@upstream --skip-emptied
 
 Then settle what the rebase left:
